{
  "_comment": [
    "Argon2id PHC strings both backends must read the same way (BOOTSTRAP.md §5.1, issue #16).",
    "`verifies`: minted by each backend, at the §5.1 cost and at another, so verification is proven in both",
    "directions and is shown to read the cost from the string rather than from the current constants.",
    "`rejects`: each must answer 'does not verify' in both backends - never an error, a panic or a 500.",
    "Both suites read this file; neither keeps a copy. Regenerate an entry by minting it with the backend",
    "The accepted shape is exactly $argon2id$v=19$m=<n>,t=<n>,p=<n>$<salt>$<hash>, unpadded standard base64.",
    "named in `minted_by`, never by editing the string."
  ],
